# Event webhook emitter (Linkly)

Before finishing, read `docs/event-webhook-setup.md` §2 (emitter) and §4.1 (checklist).

This app is an **emitter** (not a receiver). Do not ship webhook changes unless all of the following hold.

## Payload (§2.7)

Every delivery includes:

`event`, `timestamp`, `webhook_id`, `type`, `category`, `title`, `body`, `action_url`, `nexus_sso_id`, plus nested `{domain}` object where domain = first segment of `event` (e.g. `link.created` → `link: {…}`).

**Forbidden:** `recipient_user_id`, generic `context` instead of nested domain object.

## Delivery (§2.6)

- POST + `Content-Type: application/json`
- Headers: `X-Webhook-Secret`, `User-Agent: Linkly-Webhooks/1.0`
- Timeout: 10 seconds
- Non-blocking; log failures only — never roll back the primary business transaction

## Recipients (§2.5)

Resolve `nexus_sso_id` from `users` table. Separate POST per distinct recipient. Deduplicate same SSO ID. Send `nexus_sso_id: null` when no link exists.

## Config and admin (§2.1, §2.8)

- Settings key `event_webhook.webhooks[]` — multiple UUID endpoints; secret auto-gen (`whsec_`), event toggles per webhook
- Test path: `POST /api/settings/event-webhook/test` sends `webhook.test`
- `action_url` uses `FRONTEND_URL` / `config('linkly.frontend_url')`
- Secrets redacted in API responses (`secret_set: true`)

## New events (§5)

1. Name: `{domain}.{action}`
2. Add to `EventWebhookMetadata`, `SettingsService::EVENT_WEBHOOK_KEYS`, `WEBHOOK_EVENT_OPTIONS`
3. Wire trigger in `LinkWebhookService` (or domain service)
4. Update `docs/event-webhook-setup.md` Appendix A if reference implementation changes

